msgid "Vessel search"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:8
#: 59cfbcfbe73440c284b1a383d6966a29
msgid "Vessels can be searched by name, CFR, external marking, IRCS (call sign) or MMSI, including vessels which do not emit VMS. Selecting a vessel opens its sheet in the sidebar and shows its track on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:14
#: a3dfca4461ac4e61b95c3cae687c7d67
msgid "The vessel sheet has several tabs :"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:16
#: 1cd7c594b0364ab78e4545e1e8475f73
msgid "Summary tab of the vessel sheet, with the alert and beacon malfunction banners and the risk factor"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:20
#: 2e6899f7f96047449ffb248d473b9ed0
msgid "*Summary tab of the vessel sheet, with the alert and beacon malfunction banners and the risk factor*"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:22
#: f5fad5bf016e4f2e814bed939571ff8f
msgid "**Summary** (*\"Résumé\"*) : last position, current :doc:`fleet segments <fleet-segments>`, :doc:`groups <groups-of-vessels>` the vessel belongs to, the vessel's usual activity over the last year (:doc:`vessel-profiles`) and, for super users, a summary of its :doc:`risk factor <risk-factor>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:25
#: 9981cf5f856644a3824ea892f5411959
msgid "**Identity** (*\"Identité\"*) : vessel characteristics, flag state, skipper, charter status and contact methods (contact methods can be updated by super users)"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:27
#: 7a6e8102116c45269be31a1a29fce949
msgid "**Fishing** (*\"Pêche\"*) : the logbook messages of each trip (DEP, FAR, DIS, COE, COX, CRO, CPS, EOF, PNO, LAN, RTP...) with a summary of catches, the manual :doc:`prior notifications <prior-notifications>` of the trip and the transmission format of messages. Previous trips can be browsed, messages can be filtered, sorted, downloaded and displayed on the track."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:30
#: 23528e25244342638ddb857d81b2025c
msgid "**Reportings** (*\"Signalements\"*, super users) : current :doc:`reportings`, a summary of the last 12 months and the archived reportings"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:31
#: 67a24980e80b44a2b49ee6b6928126fc
msgid "**Controls** (*\"Contrôles\"*) : the history of controls by year with infractions, gears and species controlled. Each control can be opened in the :doc:`mission form <missions-and-controls>` (super users), and the trip during which a control took place can be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:33
#: 3ddfc44a1fad476dbb39fc2feff27ead
msgid "**VMS / logbook equipment** (*\"VMS/JPE\"*) : VMS and logbook equipment, satellite pictures (VisioCaptures) and the history of :doc:`beacon malfunctions <vms-beacon-monitoring>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:37
#: 69be118caacf4eae8ca4c9100144071d
msgid "Track"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:39
#: 6ab804a0834d4b27b601c6834db7bed5
msgid "The track of the selected vessel can be :"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:41
#: 0731f18edb214d0eadb60fc17cdcca56
msgid "displayed over a predefined depth (e.g. 12 hours, 1 day, 3 days...) or a custom date range"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:42
#: e33f63c3fc6d43d78be7af12e1caa236
msgid "displayed with its positions, or with the logbook messages located on the track"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:43
#: b754c22fec0f42af9142f7c81a4fffb4
msgid "exported as a CSV file"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:45
#: 0784b347a37f42d8b5aa877b79591955
msgid "AIS positions are merged into the VMS track when available."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:47
#: 714a7a38a0c84f9c99b2fddd00989d8f
msgid "Fishing tab : fleet segments and logbook messages of the current trip"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/vessel-sheet.rst:51
